00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:18,230
Oh, wow.

269
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:19,560
He's so elegant.

270
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:21,040
You're famous.

271
00:15:21,380 --> 00:15:23,498
Everybody in here is looking at you.

272
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:24,780
No, you're wrong.

273
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:26,431
They're all admiring you.

274
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:32,150
Hmm.

275
00:15:32,233 --> 00:15:33,063
So good.

276
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:35,920
This flavor.

277
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:39,460
And yes, the aroma.

278
00:15:39,800 --> 00:15:43,657
It is the unmistakable scent from
the soil of Mock of the Northland,

279
00:15:43,740 --> 00:15:46,505
bitter with plenty of
body and just a tad sour.

280
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:49,377
This wine must be...

281
00:15:49,460 --> 00:15:52,280
the famous Ituruts Burgerstein.

282
00:15:53,560 --> 00:15:54,660
Tell me, waiter.

283
00:15:55,100 --> 00:15:56,120
Am I right?

284
00:15:57,240 --> 00:15:58,100
Uh-uh.

285
00:15:58,600 --> 00:16:00,940
Not even close, sir.

286
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:03,900
Eat up.

287
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:05,940
This dish is best when hot.

288
00:16:11,180 --> 00:16:14,140
And, sir, my name's
Sanji. I'm the Zeus chef.

289
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:16,853
All the waiters ran off as of yesterday.

290
00:16:25,140 --> 00:16:26,669
You really should be fine.

291
00:16:26,780 --> 00:16:28,060
I can't help it.

292
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:29,800
He looks so confident.

293
00:16:31,220 --> 00:16:32,600
Do you know a lot?

294
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:34,960
About wine?

295
00:16:35,400 --> 00:16:36,900
Yes, I thought.

296
00:16:37,580 --> 00:16:40,580
But it seems my sense of
taste isn't working today.

297
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:43,260
What's going on?

298
00:16:43,520 --> 00:16:45,697
I'm certain I requested
that the owner serve

299
00:16:45,780 --> 00:16:48,721
that particular wine when
I made this reservation.

300
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:55,180
I can only work for one week.

301
00:16:56,440 --> 00:16:57,280
Yeah, right.

302
00:16:57,480 --> 00:16:58,540
A week, get real.

303
00:16:58,720 --> 00:16:59,700
Fine, then. Two!

304
00:16:59,940 --> 00:17:03,437
Hey, you wrecked my restaurant and
seriously injured the head chef.

305
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,617
That's a serious offense.

306
00:17:04,700 --> 00:17:08,477
You can't just settle that up with
one or two weeks of unpaid work.

307
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:11,280
That's ridiculous you win three weeks

308
00:17:12,220 --> 00:17:13,840
Talk to me?

309
00:17:27,860 --> 00:17:28,697
No deal!

310
00:17:28,780 --> 00:17:33,120
I waited ten long years
to become a pirate.

311
00:17:33,660 --> 00:17:37,580
So, I'm not gonna waste another
year stuck in this restaurant!

312
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:38,990
Hmm?

313
00:17:39,380 --> 00:17:40,380
Okay, listen.

314
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:43,457
I'm gonna get you to let
me off the hook in a week.

315
00:17:43,540 --> 00:17:45,100
That's my decision. Hmm.

316
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:48,160
If you value your time so much,

317
00:17:48,360 --> 00:17:51,637
I'll tell you what you can do
to settle your debt quickly,

318
00:17:51,720 --> 00:17:52,550
you runt.

319
00:17:53,780 --> 00:17:54,610
Oh!

320
00:17:55,020 --> 00:17:56,500
It'll cost you...

321
00:17:57,260 --> 00:17:58,340
a leg, my boy.

322
00:18:00,020 --> 00:18:01,260
Oh, that's pricey.

323
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:02,790
Heh.

324
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:04,708
Good, I got your attention.

325
00:18:14,660 --> 00:18:15,920
Waiter! Hey!

326
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:17,080
Get over here!

327
00:18:20,480 --> 00:18:24,180
I believe I've already
told you I'm not a waiter.

328
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:29,200
What an irresistible beauty you are.

329
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:34,360
My lady, would you care to join
me elsewhere for a glass of wine?

330
00:18:36,460 --> 00:18:37,880
Hey, what is this?

331
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:42,400
Is bug soup on the menu today, or did
you make it just for me? Bug soup?

332
00:18:42,820 --> 00:18:43,650
That's right.

333
00:18:43,820 --> 00:18:45,938
What's this bug doing there, waiter?

334
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:49,981
This is going to ruin the
restaurant's reputation.

335
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:52,440
Sorry, sir. Don't know, really.

336
00:18:53,080 --> 00:18:54,477
Looks like he's floating.

337
00:18:54,560 --> 00:18:59,207
Then again, it kind of looks like he's
drowning, but it's hard to say for sure.

338
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:12,720
Don't you mess with me!

339
00:19:13,760 --> 00:19:14,590
Waiter!

340
00:19:24,080 --> 00:19:27,337
You could have eaten it if you
had just taken the bug out.

341
00:19:27,420 --> 00:19:29,126
It would have been wonderful.

342
00:19:29,820 --> 00:19:33,777
It took three full days of hard
cooking to prepare that soup for you,

343
00:19:33,860 --> 00:19:34,960
and you wasted it.

344
00:19:36,080 --> 00:19:39,609
Can't you see that you're biting
off more than you can chew?

345
00:19:42,940 --> 00:19:44,400
I'm the customer here!

346
00:19:44,620 --> 00:19:45,757
Do you understand me?

347
00:19:45,840 --> 00:19:46,880
I'm paying you!

348
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:49,240
Stop it! Full Body! Shut up!

349
00:19:50,960 --> 00:19:52,640
No, Full Body, no.

350
00:19:53,720 --> 00:19:57,677
Can your money truly satisfy your hunger?

351
00:19:57,760 --> 00:20:04,480
What do you mean I'm asking
can it satisfy your hunger?

352
00:20:10,380 --> 00:20:14,674
This is getting old you're never gonna
make it if you don't just give in!

353
00:20:17,860 --> 00:20:22,320
Sometimes it's still no no respect.

354
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:38,900
Oh my it's it's Sanji
what's going on here?

355
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:42,100
Hmm, a fight.

356
00:20:52,260 --> 00:20:55,540
Don't ever waste food around me again.

357
00:20:58,920 --> 00:21:03,820
At sea, if you ever provoke your cook,
you're signing your own death warrant.

358
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:05,280
Remember that.

359
00:21:14,760 --> 00:21:15,857
Just hold it.

360
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:17,097
Almost there.

361
00:21:17,180 --> 00:21:21,237
Customer service equals love
and love equals restaurant.

362
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:24,057
The customer is the king.

363
00:21:24,140 --> 00:21:27,877
Pleasant greetings to the
customer is what it's all about.

364
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:29,557
The customer is always right!

365
00:21:29,640 --> 00:21:30,777
And we stand by that.

366
00:21:30,860 --> 00:21:32,017
Hello and welcome.

367
00:21:32,100 --> 00:21:33,037
You damn crooks!

368
00:21:33,120 --> 00:21:34,837
But don't you ever come back?

369
00:21:34,920 --> 00:21:36,720
I'm really sorry about that.

370
00:21:36,940 --> 00:21:39,240
You're all so pathetic. I laugh.

371
00:21:43,900 --> 00:21:44,980
Ah, yes, indeed.

372
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:47,177
Today will be a great day for everyone.

373
00:21:47,260 --> 00:21:49,377
Oh, hello there and
welcome, you damn crook.

374
00:21:49,460 --> 00:21:51,177
That's our service motto around here.

375
00:21:51,260 --> 00:21:52,317
No doubt about it.

376
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:53,957
The customer is our...

377
00:21:54,040 --> 00:21:56,360
Oh, no, our customer.

378
00:21:57,100 --> 00:21:58,800
Damn it, not again, Sanji.

379
00:21:59,120 --> 00:22:01,657
What do you think you're
doing to our customer?

380
00:22:01,740 --> 00:22:04,034
Can't you see he's a marine lieutenant?

381
00:22:05,060 --> 00:22:06,540
You're a terrible cook.

382
00:22:06,780 --> 00:22:09,377
What makes you think that
you can talk to me like that?

383
00:22:09,460 --> 00:22:12,600
A crappy cook like you is calling me bad?

384
00:22:13,060 --> 00:22:15,717
Restaurants can't exist
without their customers.

385
00:22:15,800 --> 00:22:19,817
They're our lifeblood, so we don't want to
hurt them the way you seem to keep doing.

386
00:22:19,900 --> 00:22:21,420
But he deserved it.

387
00:22:21,780 --> 00:22:24,780
He didn't treat the
food or me with respect.

388
00:22:25,240 --> 00:22:27,300
And he insulted all the cooks.

389
00:22:30,960 --> 00:22:33,020
So I simply taught him a lesson.

390
00:22:36,760 --> 00:22:38,360
You're gonna regret this.

391
00:22:38,660 --> 00:22:42,460
All of you, no restaurant should
treat its customers like this.

392
00:22:42,940 --> 00:22:44,240
I'll shut you down.

393
00:22:44,480 --> 00:22:45,780
Do you understand me?

394
00:22:45,920 --> 00:22:47,340
I will shut you down!

395
00:22:47,540 --> 00:22:48,940
This entire place!

396
00:22:49,120 --> 00:22:52,240
This whole restaurant is
finished! Do you hear me?

397
00:22:52,720 --> 00:22:55,680
Then, maybe I should
just finish you off now.

398
00:22:59,300 --> 00:23:01,837
Arrogant assholes like you
who think they're such big

399
00:23:01,920 --> 00:23:04,577
shots they can push anybody
around really piss me off!

400
00:23:04,660 --> 00:23:08,189
You can't keep doing this in
the restaurant every other day!

401
00:23:08,420 --> 00:23:11,380
You're not such a big
shot now, are ya? Are ya?

402
00:23:20,380 --> 00:23:21,210
What happened?

403
00:23:21,320 --> 00:23:22,150
Are they okay?

404
00:23:24,400 --> 00:23:25,680
I can breathe again!

405
00:23:25,820 --> 00:23:27,137
Boss Zef, what's happening here?

406
00:23:27,220 --> 00:23:28,557
You didn't hurt yourself, did you?

407
00:23:28,640 --> 00:23:29,470
Damn it!

408
00:23:29,780 --> 00:23:30,610
My ceiling!

409
00:23:30,860 --> 00:23:33,157
Another thing that's gonna have
to get fixed because of you!

410
00:23:33,240 --> 00:23:35,340
This is all your fault, you brat!

411
00:23:35,620 --> 00:23:36,637
How is it my fault?

412
00:23:36,720 --> 00:23:37,661
You attacked me!

413
00:23:37,760 --> 00:23:40,777
Boss, can you stop messing
around and give us a hand?

414
00:23:40,860 --> 00:23:42,540
Sanji's gone crazy again!

415
00:23:43,820 --> 00:23:44,700
Hey, Sanji!

416
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:49,297
Don't tell me you went on another
rampage in here, you idiot!

417
00:23:49,380 --> 00:23:51,060
Put a cork in it, old man!

418
00:23:51,520 --> 00:23:53,520
Oh, now you're ordering me around!

419
00:23:53,720 --> 00:23:55,557
Just who do you think you're talking to?

420
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:58,377
Do you want to sink my restaurant
to the bottom of the sea?

421
00:23:58,460 --> 00:23:59,290
You punk!

422
00:24:01,060 --> 00:24:03,860
You two, get your ass
out of my restaurant!

423
00:24:09,780 --> 00:24:12,040
What kind of restaurant is this?

424
00:24:12,380 --> 00:24:14,260
That boss is like a gangster.

425
00:24:14,780 --> 00:24:15,897
It's almost as if...

426
00:24:15,980 --> 00:24:19,120
if this were a pirate ship.

427
00:24:19,360 --> 00:24:21,577
How can you deny our customer is king?

428
00:24:21,660 --> 00:24:25,617
The only kingly customers are the ones
who stomach the slop that you call food.

429
00:24:25,700 --> 00:24:26,530
That's it.

430
00:24:26,613 --> 00:24:28,377
If you two want to fight,
you'll keep it in the kitchen.

431
00:24:28,460 --> 00:24:29,519
You understand me?

432
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:33,140
Are all these idiots really cooks?

433
00:24:34,680 --> 00:24:35,510
Lieutenant!

434
00:24:35,593 --> 00:24:36,423
Lieutenant Fullbody!

435
00:24:39,460 --> 00:24:40,760
We've got trouble!

436
00:24:41,580 --> 00:24:43,640
Wow, this restaurant is crazy.

437
00:24:43,900 --> 00:24:44,897
Sir, he's escaped!

438
00:24:44,980 --> 00:24:47,497
Pirate Creek's henchman
attacked us and vanished!

439
00:24:47,580 --> 00:24:49,297
He what? Well, sir,

440
00:24:49,380 --> 00:24:51,297
we've already lost seven of
our men and the only thing

441
00:24:51,380 --> 00:24:53,877
we wanted out of him was
a lead on fighting Creek.

442
00:24:53,960 --> 00:24:54,790
Impossible.

443
00:24:54,873 --> 00:24:56,437
When we picked him up three days ago,

444
00:24:56,520 --> 00:24:58,277
he was right on the verge
of starving to death.

445
00:24:58,360 --> 00:24:59,897
And we haven't fed him anything.

446
00:24:59,980 --> 00:25:01,277
Where did he get the strength?

447
00:25:01,360 --> 00:25:02,460
Greek pirates.

448
00:25:03,720 --> 00:25:07,137
They're the ones who are said to be
the fiercest pirates in the East Blue.

449
00:25:07,220 --> 00:25:09,860
I'm sorry, Lieutenant, I'm...

450
00:25:21,320 --> 00:25:23,640
Would seem we have a new customer, sir.

451
00:25:23,960 --> 00:25:27,960
It do well to mind his manners and
not start any trouble on my ship.

452
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:29,400
A pirate, huh?

453
00:25:42,680 --> 00:25:44,360
I don't care what it is.

454
00:25:44,520 --> 00:25:46,344
Just bring me something to eat.

455
00:25:48,460 --> 00:25:50,580
Come on, this is a restaurant.

456
00:25:50,960 --> 00:25:52,980
Hello and welcome, you damn crook!

457
00:25:54,320 --> 00:25:56,377
I'm just gonna say this one more time.

458
00:25:56,460 --> 00:25:58,677
and bring me something
to eat and make it quick.

459
00:25:58,760 --> 00:26:00,740
That cook is gonna get us killed.

460
00:26:00,980 --> 00:26:02,217
Of course, right away,

461
00:26:02,300 --> 00:26:06,182
but might I be so bold to inquire
how you're paying for your meal?

462
00:26:08,940 --> 00:26:10,500
Will a bullet be enough?

463
00:26:10,660 --> 00:26:12,601
So you don't have any money then?

464
00:26:14,040 --> 00:26:16,400
That dumbass Patty broke into the chair.

465
00:26:16,900 --> 00:26:18,140
Whoa, what power.

466
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:23,765
Sorry, pirate, but our policy is
to only serve paying customers.

467
00:26:24,220 --> 00:26:26,660
Kick his ass, Paddy! Show that, pirate!

468
00:26:26,840 --> 00:26:28,487
We cooks don't screw around!

469
00:26:29,920 --> 00:26:33,214
Oh, I can hear your stomach
grumbling from here, pirate.

470
00:26:33,500 --> 00:26:35,240
That was a fart, jerk.

471
00:26:35,520 --> 00:26:38,420
Now listen, get me something to eat now.

472
00:26:38,800 --> 00:26:41,600
We're not getting you
anything, so beat it!

473
00:26:46,940 --> 00:26:48,740
I can't take it anymore.

474
00:26:49,060 --> 00:26:51,017
All of these cooks are insane.

475
00:26:51,100 --> 00:26:52,747
I've got to get out of here.

476
00:26:52,980 --> 00:26:56,215
I don't want anything to do
with this place ever again.

477
00:26:56,760 --> 00:26:57,860
Kick him! Come on!

478
00:26:59,960 --> 00:27:02,080
And now, you damn crooks!

479
00:27:02,520 --> 00:27:04,820
If you need anything, just ask, okay?

480
00:27:09,480 --> 00:27:11,420
And please, never come back!

481
00:27:16,580 --> 00:27:17,410
Dammit!

482
00:27:17,493 --> 00:27:20,476
If I wasn't so weak from
hunger, I'd be inside eating.

483
00:27:40,780 --> 00:27:43,900
How beautiful and cruel this ocean can be.

484
00:27:44,280 --> 00:27:48,162
It's almost a death sentence to
lose your food and water out here.

485
00:27:48,320 --> 00:27:50,360
How difficult it is to survive.

486
00:27:51,100 --> 00:27:54,737
I know what it means to go hungry
because of the sea more than anyone.

487
00:27:54,820 --> 00:27:57,114
You can die for your pride if you want.

488
00:27:58,680 --> 00:28:00,740
But listen, if you eat and survive,

489
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:02,657
won't that give you the
opportunity to fight for

490
00:28:02,740 --> 00:28:05,505
pride truly worth having
now and in the future?

491
00:28:19,440 --> 00:28:20,320
I'm sorry.

492
00:28:21,840 --> 00:28:22,900
I'm sorry.

493
00:28:23,140 --> 00:28:24,199
Thank you so much.

494
00:28:24,420 --> 00:28:25,800
I thought it was over.

495
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:28,059
I truly thought I was going to die.

496
00:28:32,740 --> 00:28:35,280
This fruit, it's delicious.

497
00:28:35,600 --> 00:28:38,080
I've never eaten food this good before.

498
00:28:43,640 --> 00:28:45,180
Of course it is.

499
00:28:46,920 --> 00:28:49,060
I think I just found my cook.

500
00:28:50,100 --> 00:28:52,117
You're lucky he gave you some food.

501
00:28:52,200 --> 00:28:54,200
You weren't looking so good there.

502
00:28:55,060 --> 00:28:57,820
I thought you were a goner. So listen, Mr.

503
00:28:57,940 --> 00:29:01,058
Cook, why don't you leave
this boat and join my crew?

504
00:29:01,500 --> 00:29:04,206
I could use a cook like
you on my pirate ship.

505
00:29:04,760 --> 00:29:05,590
Huh? Huh?

506
00:29:19,060 --> 00:29:21,257
That I knew would lead me.

507
00:29:21,340 --> 00:29:25,437
I had to find my way to that place.

508
00:29:25,520 --> 00:29:28,337
Before someone could beat me!

509
00:29:28,420 --> 00:29:32,517
The promised land was in my grasp.

510
00:29:32,600 --> 00:29:35,200
And I wouldn't let go.

511
00:29:36,360 --> 00:29:38,997
La la la la la?

512
00:29:39,080 --> 00:29:40,417
My only dream.

513
00:29:43,560 --> 00:29:48,140
I won't stop chasing
it until it comes true.

514
00:29:50,020 --> 00:29:56,917
But if the world ever
changes, I call out your name.

515
00:29:57,000 --> 00:30:03,500
We can return to the time
when everything's the same.

516
00:30:04,220 --> 00:30:10,540
As long as I'm with you,
my memories won't fade.

517
00:30:11,280 --> 00:30:15,860
Waiting for that one true dream?
